course: dictionary
lesson: 12356
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «crib» is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. This is the context, and it leaves clues. «The baby slept soundly in her crib.» The baby and sleeping tell you a crib is a bed here.
explain: «At Christmas, the family set up the crib in the hall, with Mary, Joseph and the baby.» Christmas and the figures tell you this crib is a model of the stable where Jesus was born. Always ask: what do the other words tell me about where and when this is happening?
explain: «Ben was caught with a crib sheet in his pocket during the spelling test.» A crib sheet is a paper of answers used to cheat, and the test tells you this crib is about cheating. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Crib» can mean a baby's bed with high barred sides. This is the word for US and Canada; in the UK it is called a «cot».
fact: «Crib» can mean a model of the stable where Jesus was born, set up at Christmas. This is also called a nativity scene.
fact: «Crib» can mean to copy someone else's work and pretend it is yours. This is cheating, and it is punished at school.
fact: «Crib» can also be slang for someone's home, as in «Welcome to my crib», and it is informal.
exercise: «The baby slept soundly in her crib.» In the UK, what would you call this bed? | *Cot | Crib sheet | Cribbage | Stable
exercise: «At Christmas, the family set up the crib with Mary, Joseph and the baby.» What is the crib here? | A wooden box of food for animals | A card game | *A model of the stable where Jesus was born | A bed for babies with high sides
exercise: «Ruby was caught cribbing in the maths test and lost all her marks.» What does cribbing mean? | Helping the teacher mark the papers | *Copying someone else's work and pretending it is her own | Singing loudly at the front of the class
test: «Welcome to my crib, it is the best place on the street!» What does crib mean here? | A model stable | A card game | Baby's bed | *Home
test: «Dad wrote the answers on a crib sheet before the quiz.» What does crib sheet suggest? | A map of the stable | A list of Christmas songs | A bed for a baby | *Notes or answers, sometimes used to cheat
exam: «The farmer filled the crib with hay for the cows.» What is a crib here? | A baby's bed | A model of the stable at Christmas | A card game | *A wooden box or rack that holds food for animals
